  "author": "A Robot",
  "institution": "MTSU",
  "courseName": "Introductory Molecular Biology",
  "estimatedLength": "45 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Identify the structural components of DNA, including the sugar-phosphate backbone, nitrogenous bases, and hydrogen bonds, and explain how these form the double helix.",
    "Apply complementary base-pairing rules to determine a complementary DNA strand and relate pair identity to hydrogen-bond count.",
    "Describe DNA strand antiparallelism and the 5'-to-3' directionality of DNA backbones.",
    "Trace the functions of helicase, single-strand binding proteins, DNA polymerase, and DNA ligase at a replication fork.",
    "Explain why leading- and lagging-strand synthesis differ and how Okazaki fragments arise from DNA polymerase directionality.",
    "Predict the semiconservative outcome of one and two rounds of DNA replication."
  ],
